===Etymology===
First recorded 1597; from {{m|en|upholster|pos=noun}} or {{af|en|upholsterer|alt1=upholster''(''er'')''|-ery|alt2=-''(''er'')''y}} or {{af|en|-y}}.<ref>{{R:Oxford English Dictionary|entry=Upho·lstery|volume=X|part=1|page=426|column=3|passage=f. {{smallcaps|Upholster}} ''sb.''|nodot=1}}</ref><ref>{{R:Collins English Dictionary|source=Webster|passage=see upholsterer & -ery}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com|passage=upholster(er) + -y<sup>3</sup>}}</ref><ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|passage=see upholster + -y (4).|nodot=1}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʌpˈhəʊlstəɹi/|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[craft]] or [[business]] of [[upholster]]ing [[furniture]].
# The [[material]]s used in upholstering furniture.

